{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction"],"declarations":23,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bringFiberAction_canonicalClassAngles","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.bringFiberAction_canonicalClassAngles","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L174-L185","doc":"**The canonical class-angle map furnishes a `BringFiberAction`** whose rotation angles are the\ngenuine icosahedral conjugacy-class angles. Provided as a `def` (not a global `instance`) to avoid\nclashing with the merged Reeb-phase instance `bringFiberAction_icosahedral` (#3093); the two are\ndifferent-but-both-injective angle assignments, and this one is the geometrically canonical\n(actual-rotation-angle) realization. `five_distinct_classes` reduces to `irrepClassAngle_injective`\nthrough the injective `ℕ ↪ ℝ` cast. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_angle_map_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_angle_map_unique","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L139-L172","doc":"**Uniqueness — the three structural properties force the canonical map.** Any class assignment\n`f` that is character-nonvanishing (P1), Galois 5-fold chiral (`T₁ ↦ c5a`, `T₂ ↦ c5b`, P2),\ntrivial-to-identity (`A ↦ e`, P3), and injective, equals `canonicalClassMap`. In particular the\n`G ↦ c3` / `H ↦ c2` split (the G-vs-T₂ tie) is forced: with `A, T₁, T₂` placed, `G` must avoid\n`c2` (`χ_G = 0` there, by P1) and `e, c5a, c5b` (already taken, by injectivity), leaving only `c3`;\nthen `H` lands on the last free class `c2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_satisfies_nonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonical_satisfies_nonvanishing","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L136-L137","doc":"The canonical map is character-nonvanishing (P1 holds). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SatisfiesNonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SatisfiesNonvanishing","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L131-L134","doc":"**(P1) Character-nonvanishing predicate** on a class assignment `f`. `abbrev` so that the\n`∀ l, … = false` body stays transparently `Decidable` (over `Fintype A5Irrep`) for `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle_injective","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L126-L129","doc":"**The five class angles are distinct** — the substantive `five_distinct_classes` content, now with\nthe actual icosahedral conjugacy-class angles `{0,72,120,144,180}` rather than the continuous Reeb\nphases of #3093. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonicalClassMap_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonicalClassMap_injective","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L123-L124","doc":"**The canonical class map is a genuine bijection** (injective on the five-element `A5Irrep`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle_values","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle_values","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L118-L121","doc":"The five class angles, explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.irrepClassAngle","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L115-L116","doc":"**The canonical class-angle bijection in degrees**: `A↦0, T₁↦72, G↦120, T₂↦144, H↦180`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonicalClassMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.canonicalClassMap","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**The canonical class map** `A₅ irrep → conjugacy class`, uniquely forced by P1+P2+P3\n(`canonical_angle_map_unique`). The `G-vs-T₂` tie is resolved: `G ↦ c3`, `T₂ ↦ c5b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.charVanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.charVanishes","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L95-L104","doc":"**The A₅ character zero pattern** (`charVanishes λ C = true ⟺ χ_λ(C) = 0`): `T₁,T₂` vanish on\nthe 3-cycles `c3`; `G` vanishes on the double-transpositions `c2`; `H` vanishes on both 5-cycle\nclasses `c5a, c5b`; the trivial rep `A` never vanishes. The only character datum the determination\nuses (no `√5`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.angle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.angle","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L91-L93","doc":"The icosahedral rotation angle (in degrees) of each conjugacy class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instFintypeA5Irrep_folio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instFintypeA5Irrep_folio","kind":"instance","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L87-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instFintypeIcoClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instFintypeIcoClass","kind":"instance","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.allList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.allList","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L80-L81","doc":"All five icosahedral conjugacy classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprIcoClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprIcoClass","kind":"instance","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprIcoClass.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprIcoClass.repr","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqIcoClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqIcoClass","kind":"instance","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L78-L78","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c5b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c5b","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c5a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c5a","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c3","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.c2","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.e","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass.e","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcoClass","kind":"inductive","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/KeystoneCanonicalAngleMap.lean#L73-L78","doc":"The five conjugacy classes of `A₅ ≅ I ⊂ SO(3)`, named by their rotation order:\n`e` (identity), `c2` (double transpositions, order 2), `c3` (3-cycles, order 3),\n`c5a`/`c5b` (the two 5-cycle classes, Galois-conjugate). ","signatureChunk":0}]}